msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:164
msgid "Distinctive Vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:165
msgid "Find words used at higher relative rates in one country or decade than in the remaining newspaper articles. A second view identifies periods of increased use of subject tags. Statistical thresholds are explained alongside the charts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:178
msgid "Loading distinctive vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:184
msgid "Entity Networks"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:185
msgid "Explore links between people, organisations, places, subjects and events recorded on the same items. Shared records indicate catalogue associations, which require interpretation through the sources."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:197
msgid "Loading entity networks"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:203
msgid "Index Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:204
msgid "Explore the catalogue index and the use of subject and place tags over time. Counts describe recorded associations rather than word occurrences in the original texts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:219
msgid "Loading index overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:225
msgid "Laïcité"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:226
msgid "Explore a dossier selected through the Laïcité subject tag and vocabulary in titles and available full text, including YouTube transcripts. Compare source types, terms in context, associated entries and AI ratings. Descriptive fields are excluded from vocabulary counts; extracts follow each field’s public status."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:262
msgid "Loading laïcité dossier"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:269
msgid "Press Language"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:270
msgid "Compare estimated reading ease, vocabulary diversity and article length over time and by newspaper. Measures use extracted text; the charts explain the scores and their limitations."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:280
msgid "Loading press language metrics"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:286
msgid "On This Day"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:287
msgid "Show articles and periodical issues published on today’s date in earlier years. Switch between Gregorian and converted Islamic-calendar dates, and between list, decade and clipping layouts. Only records with suitable dates can appear."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:293
msgid "Islamic Organisations Co-occurrence"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:294
msgid "Compare pairs of words found near the names of selected Islamic organisations in newspaper articles. Darker cells indicate pairs found together in more articles."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:305
msgid "Loading organisation co-occurrences"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:311
msgid "Periodicals Semantic Landscape"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:312
msgid "Explore Islamic periodical issues arranged by an AI comparison of their tables of contents. Nearby points suggest issues to compare; positions and distances are approximate."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:325 src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:460
msgid "Loading semantic landscape"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:331
msgid "Periodicals Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:332
msgid "Explore Islamic periodical holdings by year, publication, country, language and catalogue subject, with vocabulary and statistically modelled themes. Gaps in the collection do not establish gaps in publication."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:343
msgid "Loading periodicals overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:351
msgid "Pipeline Explainer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:352
msgid "Explain one IWAC processing workflow — topic modelling, OCR with AI, entity extraction and metadata enrichment, the Albani Zaria sermons analysis, tables of contents for Islamic publications, Ask AI or press attitudes — as a short animated diagram with captions. It uses illustrative examples and requests no data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:359
msgid "Press Bylines"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:360
msgid "Explore recorded journalists and press agencies, the share of articles with a byline, and their representation over time. A missing byline may reflect incomplete cataloguing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:371
msgid "Loading press bylines"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:377
msgid "Press Reprints"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:378
msgid "Find articles from different newspapers with highly similar AI text representations. These candidate pairs may indicate shared dispatches, communiqués or reprints; read both articles before concluding that copying occurred."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:390
msgid "Loading press reprints"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:396
msgid "References Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:397
msgid "Explore the bibliography by publication date, type, language, associated country, author and subject. Additional views show authorship links, available full text, modelled themes and text similarity."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:410
msgid "Loading references overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:416
msgid "Scary Terms"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:417
msgid "Explore selected vocabulary associated with radicalism and extremism in newspaper articles: occurrences, trends, countries, term pairs, surrounding vocabulary and tagged places. Counts describe language use, not the extremism of the people discussed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:439
msgid "Loading scary terms"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:446
msgid "Semantic Landscape"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:447
msgid "Explore newspaper articles arranged by an AI comparison of their full texts, with colours for country, decade or modelled topic. Nearby points suggest texts to compare; distances are approximate."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:466
msgid "Sentiment Atlas"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:467
msgid "Compare AI assessments of tone towards Islam and Muslims, their prominence in articles, and subjectivity. Views show changes over time, differences between sources and model agreement. Ratings require checking against the texts, especially for subjectivity."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:479
msgid "Loading sentiment atlas"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:485
msgid "Spatial Exploration"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:486
msgid "Map places linked through catalogue records, with filters for countries and associated people, organisations, subjects or events. Only places with coordinates appear; the map does not include every location mentioned in the texts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:497
msgid "Loading spatial exploration"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:503
msgid "Term Trends"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:504
msgid "Compare the number or share of dated newspaper articles containing selected words. Search the frequent-word vocabulary and compare up to eight terms. Each word counts once per article, and only articles with usable processed text enter the calculation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:515
msgid "Loading term trends"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:521
msgid "Topic Explorer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:522
msgid "Explore the themes a statistical topic model identifies in newspaper articles. Select a theme to examine its publication dates, countries, newspapers and example articles. Modelled themes differ from catalogue subject tags."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/BlockRegistry.php:543
msgid "Loading Topic Explorer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:37
msgid "Topic modelling (LDA)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:38
msgid "OCR with AI"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:39
msgid "Entity extraction and metadata enrichment"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:40
msgid "Albani Zaria sermons: from recordings to figures"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:41
msgid "Tables of contents for Islamic publications"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:42
msgid "Ask AI: from a question to a cited answer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:43
msgid "Press attitudes: how language models rate the articles"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:48
msgid "How topic modelling finds themes in the articles"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:49
msgid "IWAC trains a statistical topic model, Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA), on the text of its newspaper articles. The model is never told what the topics are: it finds groups of words that tend to appear in the same articles."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:55 src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:341
msgid "Articles"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:56
msgid "The input is the OCR text of each French-language newspaper article."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:57
msgid "Islamic publications and scholarly references have models of their own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:61
msgid "Text preparation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:62
msgid "Words are reduced to their dictionary form, and very common words are removed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:63
msgid "Place names and other terms that would dominate every topic are set aside; frequent word pairs such as al_azhar stay together."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:67
msgid "Word counts"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:68
msgid "Each article becomes a count of the words it uses; word order is discarded."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:69
msgid "Words found in very few articles, or in a large share of them, are left out."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:73
msgid "Topic discovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:74
msgid "LDA infers 30 topics, each a list of words weighted by how strongly they belong to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:75
msgid "A topic’s label is simply its most characteristic words."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:79
msgid "Topic mixtures"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:80
msgid "Each article receives a share of several topics; IWAC keeps its main topic and its three strongest."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:81
msgid "The Topic Explorer follows each topic across years, countries and newspapers."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:85
msgid "Topics are patterns inferred from words that occur together, not subjects assigned by a cataloguer. They need interpretation: read the articles behind a topic before naming it, and remember that most articles combine several topics."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:86
msgid "Illustrative example: the words and proportions in the drawings are invented to show the method, not taken from the IWAC model."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:89
msgid "How AI turns scanned pages into searchable text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:90
msgid "IWAC uses one of two routes, depending on what a document already has. New scans go to a multimodal model that reads the page image itself; noisy text from conventional OCR can be corrected instead. A document takes one route, not both."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:94
msgid "Direct extraction, the current workflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:98
msgid "Scanned page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:99
msgid "The document’s PDF goes to a multimodal model: Gemini reads it page by page, Mistral Document AI in a single request."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:103
msgid "Reading order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:104
msgid "The instructions set the order: main columns left to right and top to bottom, then headings, captions and sidebars."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:105
msgid "The model reads layout and text in one pass; the steps are drawn apart here."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:109
msgid "Transcription"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:110
msgid "The model writes out the text, rejoining lines and words that the columns broke, and keeps the source wording."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:114
msgid "Assembled text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:115
msgid "The pages are joined with page markers and, after a preview, saved to the record with the name of the model."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:116
msgid "The scan stays beside the text: an unusual layout can still come out in the wrong order."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:122
msgid "Post-correction of noisy OCR"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:126
msgid "Noisy OCR text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:127
msgid "Text from conventional OCR, with its misread characters, broken words and encoding errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:131
msgid "Sections"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:132
msgid "A very long text is cut into sections that the model can correct in one request."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:133
msgid "Context across a cut can be lost."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:137
msgid "AI correction"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:138
msgid "A language model fixes recognition errors and restores accents, without translating or modernising the text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:142
msgid "Corrected text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:143
msgid "The corrected version becomes the searchable full text; the original OCR is kept for comparison."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:144
msgid "Historical names and spellings are kept as printed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:149
msgid "Fluent output is not proof of accuracy. A model can modernise an unusual spelling, guess a missing word or skip part of a page, and an error in fluent text is harder to spot than garbled characters. Check quotations and proper names against the scan."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:150
msgid "Illustrative example: the page and its misreadings are invented to show the method."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:153
msgid "How names in articles become links to authority records"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:154
msgid "An AI model reads each newspaper article and lists the persons, organisations, places and subjects it mentions. A name is only a mention until it is matched with IWAC’s authority files, which gather variant spellings under one record."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:160
msgid "Extraction and normalisation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:161
msgid "The model lists the names it finds, without titles such as El Hadj and with acronyms written out in full."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:162
msgid "Subjects are chosen from IWAC’s own vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:166
msgid "Reconciliation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:167
msgid "Each name is compared with the authority records and their alternative forms: exact matches are accepted, close spellings only suggested."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:168
msgid "A name that fits several records is set aside rather than guessed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:172
msgid "Review"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:173
msgid "A researcher checks ambiguous names, close spellings and unknown entities, and accepts, corrects or rejects each proposal."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:174
msgid "A name with no record waits for a new authority record, created after curation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:178
msgid "Linking"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:179
msgid "Confirmed matches are added to the article as links: places under Spatial coverage, everything else under Subject."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:180
msgid "Each link records the model that proposed it; an update only adds links, after a backup."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:184
msgid "A highlighted name is a mention, not yet a link. A model can miss a name or match it to the wrong record, and the renamings and splits of organisations need historical knowledge, so uncertain matches are reviewed and every update can be reversed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:185
msgid "Illustrative example: the name variants are those of a real person in the IWAC index; the sentence around them is invented."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:192
msgid "How the Albani Zaria sermons become figures"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:193
msgid "The Albani Zaria exhibition counts words, terms and names across the transcribed sermons and lessons of Shaykh Muhammad Auwal Albani Zaria. Every figure leads back to a passage, and every passage to its recording."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:201
msgid "The recordings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:202
msgid "Speech recognition writes each recording out word for word, in 20-minute segments, and estimates who is speaking. Recordings not yet transcribed, and passages in English, are left out."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:203
msgid "Both can be wrong, so every passage links back to the recording."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:207
msgid "Vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:208
msgid "Spellings with and without the hooked letters (ɓ, ɗ, ƙ, ƴ) count as one word; the commonest words and the speaker’s fillers, such as wato, are left out."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:209
msgid "The stop words are those published by Bashir, Bichi and Adamu (2024); religious formulae are counted as whole phrases, and a simple rule tells Arabic passages from Hausa."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:213
msgid "People and places"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:214
msgid "A named-entity model proposed names once; only a list of names and spellings curated by hand is counted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:215
msgid "A spelling with another meaning, such as shehu, is left out, so the counts are floors."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:219
msgid "Youth and politics"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:220
msgid "Terms for youth and for politics are found in the text, with the words that occur unusually often near them and the places where the two themes meet."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:221
msgid "The word lists are a draft that a Hausa-speaking specialist will check."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:225
msgid "Figures and passages"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:226
msgid "The counts become the page’s charts, its map and the words that set each recording apart; passages are quoted only from transcripts that are public."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:227
msgid "A count shows where to look; the passage and the recording are the evidence."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:231
msgid "The figures describe these recordings only: one preacher, the part of his teaching transcribed so far, and the errors the transcription contains. The word lists and translations are drafts awaiting a specialist’s review."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:232
msgid "Illustrative example: the drawings show the method with words the exhibition’s method section cites; the passages are lines, not quotations."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:240
msgid "How an issue of an Islamic magazine gets its table of contents"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:241
msgid "Digitised Islamic magazines were first searchable only as whole issues. An AI model reads each issue page by page, follows every article across the pages it spans, and writes a table of contents that makes each article findable on its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:247
msgid "Issue"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:248
msgid "Each digitised issue is split into single pages, and each page goes to a vision model on its own: Gemini, Claude or Mistral OCR."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:249
msgid "The issue itself stays whole in the collection."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:253
msgid "Articles on each page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:254
msgid "The model lists every article on the page: its title as printed, with its section in brackets, its authors and a short summary of what the page shows."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:255
msgid "Covers, advertisements and short notices are set aside; Arabic terms read correctly are kept."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:259
msgid "Continuations"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:260
msgid "Markers such as “suite page 7” or “à suivre” are noted, so the parts of an article printed apart can be found again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:261
msgid "An article that ends on a later page is listed there too, under its title or as a continuation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:265
msgid "Consolidation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:266
msgid "A second pass merges the parts of each article, gathers its pages and authors, and writes one summary of four to six sentences."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:267
msgid "Parts are joined by title, by continuation markers and by subject; a long series in several parts may not merge correctly."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:271 src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:399
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:272
msgid "The index is saved to the issue’s Table of contents field: one entry per article, with its pages, title, authors and summary."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:273
msgid "The model that wrote it is recorded with the field; an update changes nothing else, after a backup and a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:277
msgid "A table of contents read by a model guides a reader through the issue; it is not a catalogue record. An unusual layout can hide an article or turn an advertisement into one, a decorative heading can pass for a title, and every summary is selective: read the pages before citing an article."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:278
msgid "Illustrative example: the issue, its titles and its pages are invented to show the method."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:286
msgid "How an AI assistant answers a question with IWAC"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:287
msgid "The IWAC MCP server lets an AI assistant you already use search the collection for you. The server supplies records and figures, read-only; the assistant plans the searches, reads what comes back and writes the answer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:293
msgid "Your question"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:294
msgid "You ask in any language, in Claude, ChatGPT or another assistant connected to IWAC; the assistant decides which IWAC tools to call."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:295
msgid "Most sources are in French, so the instructions have it search in French, with spelling variants, whatever language you write in."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:299
msgid "Tool calls"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:300
msgid "The server offers 39 read-only tools: search the collection, read one record, look up a person or a place, count over time, compare countries."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:301
msgid "Built-in instructions, and an optional research skill, tell the assistant how to search, read and cite."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:305
msgid "The dataset"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:306
msgid "Each call is answered from IWAC’s research dataset on Hugging Face; the Claude Desktop extension keeps a copy on your computer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:307
msgid "Search matches the words of the metadata and the OCR text, so a misread word stays hidden."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:311
msgid "Results with their sources"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:312
msgid "Each result comes back with the link to its IWAC record, and each call records the version of the dataset that answered it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:313
msgid "A warning says when a list was cut short or a kind of material could not be searched."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:317
msgid "The answer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:318
msgid "The assistant may search again or open records, then writes the answer, citing each source by its IWAC link."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:319
msgid "The wording is the model’s, not IWAC’s: follow the links before relying on a claim."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:323
msgid "The server returns records; the assistant interprets them. A count describes what IWAC holds, not everything that was ever published, and an assistant can miss a spelling variant or misread a source: open the linked records before quoting them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:324
msgid "Illustrative example: the question, the tool calls and the results in the drawings are invented to show the method."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:334
msgid "How language models rate the press’s portrayal of Islam"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:335
msgid "Several large language models read the same newspaper articles, and each rates on its own how central Islam and Muslims are to an article, how positively or negatively they are portrayed, and how subjective the writing is."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:342
msgid "The OCR text of each French- or English-language newspaper article is sent whole, one article at a time."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:343
msgid "Articles in Ewé, Kabiyè or Dendi, or with no language recorded, are left out: a few dozen in all."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:347
msgid "One task, several models"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:348
msgid "Every model receives the same instructions, in French, and rates the article independently of the others."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:349
msgid "Their settings are not identical: temperature and reasoning effort follow each provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:353
msgid "Three ratings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:354
msgid "Centrality runs from very central to not addressed, polarity from very positive to very negative, subjectivity from very objective to very subjective."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:355
msgid "When Islam is not addressed, polarity is “not applicable” and subjectivity is left empty."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:359
msgid "Justifications"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:360
msgid "Each rating comes with a sentence or two citing the article, and every model’s ratings are saved to the article’s record, apart."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:361
msgid "An article’s page shows each model’s reasoning beside its rating."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:365
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:366
msgid "The atlas follows each model across years, countries, topics and newspapers, and measures how often the models agree."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:367
msgid "The atlas takes no majority vote: where the models disagree, the disagreement is shown."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:371
msgid "The ratings are model outputs, not facts about the articles. The models agree most on centrality and least on subjectivity, one model reads centrality differently from the rest, and a model asked again can change its answer: read the article and the justification before drawing a conclusion."
msgstr ""

#: src/Site/PipelinePresets.php:372
msgid "Illustrative example: the article, the ratings and the agreement in the drawings are invented to show the method."
msgstr ""

